  "title": "Before Jumping to Conclusions, Focus on the General Information",
  "description": "Before jumping to conclusions, focus on the general information. Here’s how: - Check the base rate: Ask, “What do the overall statistics say?” - Pause before judging: Look for the larger trends instead of just the specifics. - Combine both perspectives: Use general information to inform the specific case. Example: If 90% of a population recovers from an illness, don’t let one extreme story make you believe the illness is fatal.",
